---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How America Back to God Mission collects, uses and protects information when you use this website."
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {site.name} (the "Mission," "we," or "us") collects, uses, and shares information
    when you visit this website (the "Site"), contact us, or sign up as a member or volunteer.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <p>
    When you contact us, become a member, or volunteer, you may give us your name, email address, phone number, and the
    message or details you choose to include. Volunteer forms may ask for additional details such as your address or
    availability. These forms are provided through Google Forms. If you call or email us directly, we receive the
    information you share in that conversation.
  </p>
  <h3>Donation-related information</h3>
  <p>
    Online giving is not currently available on the Site. If we add it, donations will be handled by a third-party
    payment processor. The processor collects your payment details directly, and we will not receive or store your full
    card number. We may receive limited information such as your name, email address, and the amount of your gift.
  </p>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider (Vercel) may process technical information such as your IP address, browser type, the pages you
    request, and the time of your visit in server logs. This is used to deliver, secure, and troubleshoot the Site. We do
    not currently run analytics or advertising trackers on the Site. If we add basic analytics in the future, we will
    update this policy first.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your questions and messages.</li>
    <li>To process membership and volunteer requests.</li>
    <li>To send members monthly emails with updates on the best way to pray, and information about our events.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve the Site.</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

  <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The Site itself does not set cookies for tracking or advertising. Embedded content from other services, such as a
    Google Form, may set its own cookies when you load or use it. We do not control those cookies. You can block or
    delete cookies in your browser settings, though some embedded content may not work as expected.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>We rely on the following services, each with its own privacy practices:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Forms</strong> collects form submissions on our behalf. See
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the Site.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube</strong> are linked from the Site. When you follow those links you leave
      the Site and their policies apply.
    </li>
    <li><strong>A payment processor</strong> will be named here if and when online giving is added.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. How we share information</h2>
  <p>
    We share information only with service providers that help us run the Site and our programs, when the law requires
    it, or with your consent. We do not sell or rent your information.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep messages and form responses for as long as we need them to respond to you and to run the programs you asked
    to join. For example, we keep a member's email address until they unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. When
    information is no longer needed, we delete it or remove details that identify you. Server logs are kept by our
    hosting provider under its own retention schedule.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If
    you believe a child has given us personal information, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You may contact us at any time to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask what personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct or delete your information.</li>
    <li>Stop receiving emails from us. Every email can be answered with a request to unsubscribe.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under your state's law. Contact us and we will respond
    as soon as we reasonably can.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect the information we hold. No method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page shows when it last
    changed.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your information:<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`}>{site.phone}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
